WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.427
Sometimes a table is convenient for people to read but awkward for analysis.

00:00:05.427 --> 00:00:10.287
The starting table has separate quiz1 and quiz2 columns.

00:00:10.287 --> 00:00:17.933
Melt turns those column names into values inside a new quiz column, with the scores placed in one score column.

00:00:18.485 --> 00:00:22.897
Each student now has multiple rows—one row per quiz.

00:00:22.897 --> 00:00:29.632
This long format is often easier for grouping, plotting, and statistical analysis.

00:00:29.632 --> 00:00:34.566
Think of melt as moving information from column headers down into rows.
